WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.085 --> 00:00:05.469
Tom wanted to return to the prince's room and eat nuts.

2
00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:09.073
But first he had to deal with his itchy nose.

3
00:00:09.074 --> 00:00:12.562
So he continued to sit at the table.

4
00:00:12.563 --> 00:00:17.501
He wrinkled his nose, trying to get rid of the annoying sensation.

5
00:00:17.502 --> 00:00:21.231
But that only made him want to sneeze.

6
00:00:21.232 --> 00:00:28.699
As Tom's eyes began to water, his distress became obvious to everyone in the room.

7
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:33.148
"Do you need some assistance, sir?" the royal taster asked.

8
00:00:33.149 --> 00:00:37.306
"Was there something wrong with the food?"

9
00:00:37.307 --> 00:00:41.714
"There was nothing wrong with the food," the head chef snapped.

10
00:00:41.715 --> 00:00:46.384
"I sampled all the dishes myself before they were brought to the table.

11
00:00:46.385 --> 00:00:50.583
Everything was delicious!"

12
00:00:50.584 --> 00:00:58.216
"Perhaps you need more water?" The royal cupbearer filled Tom's cup again.

13
00:00:58.217 --> 00:01:01.731
Tom needed to do something right now!

14
00:01:01.732 --> 00:01:06.013
He beckoned for Lord Hertford to approach the table.

15
00:01:06.014 --> 00:01:12.611
"What's the matter, Your Highness?" Lord Hertford's face was full of concern.

16
00:01:12.612 --> 00:01:15.621
"My nose itches terribly.

17
00:01:15.622 --> 00:01:20.984
I have so many servants that there has to be one in charge of my nose.

18
00:01:20.985 --> 00:01:26.429
Please summon the royal nose scratcher immediately."

19
00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:33.173
"I'm sorry, sir, but there is no royal nose scratcher," Lord Hertford said.

20
00:01:33.174 --> 00:01:39.419
"No royal nose scratcher?" By now the tears were streaming down Tom's face.

21
00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:43.312
"Then what am I supposed to do?"

22
00:01:43.313 --> 00:01:45.913
Lord Hertford was baffled.

23
00:01:45.914 --> 00:01:51.557
"Surely this isn't the first time in your life that your nose has itched.

24
00:01:51.558 --> 00:01:55.571
What have you done in the past?"

25
00:01:55.572 --> 00:02:01.101
"When I was on Offal . . . " Tom remembered the king's orders.

26
00:02:01.102 --> 00:02:04.385
"Oh, I don't care what the proper thing is.

27
00:02:04.386 --> 00:02:08.123
I need to scratch my own nose!"

28
00:02:08.124 --> 00:02:12.789
And that's exactly what he did.

29
00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:16.214
No one gasped or laughed.

30
00:02:16.215 --> 00:02:21.551
Lord Hertford was just relieved that Tom hadn't said anything more about Offal Street.

31
00:02:21.552 --> 00:02:30.273
"Very good, Your Highness," Lord Hertford said, and the servants broke into applause.

32
00:02:30.274 --> 00:02:35.542
The royal napkin holder arrived with a gold bowl filled with rose water.

33
00:02:35.543 --> 00:02:39.083
Over his arm he carried a napkin.

34
00:02:39.084 --> 00:02:44.703
Tom was supposed to wash and dry his hands after meals, but he didn't know that.

35
00:02:44.704 --> 00:02:49.654
He raised the dish to his lips and solemnly took a drink.

36
00:02:49.655 --> 00:02:52.488
"It doesn't have much flavor."

37
00:02:52.489 --> 00:02:56.688
Tom handed the bowl back to the royal napkin holder.

38
00:02:56.689 --> 00:03:01.367
"Please make it stronger next time," he said to the head chef.

39
00:03:01.368 --> 00:03:07.273
She started to protest, but Tom stood up, which signaled that lunch was over. Tom

40
00:03:07.274 --> 00:03:13.837
announced that he wanted to return to his room. "I'd

41
00:03:13.838 --> 00:03:19.739
like to be left alone for the rest of the afternoon," he said. As

42
00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:25.539
soon as his door closed, Tom began hunting for a nutcracker. "Prince

43
00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:31.140
Edward has everything, so he must have a nutcracker." But

44
00:03:31.141 --> 00:03:37.192
before he found one, he was distracted by shelves full of books. One

45
00:03:37.193 --> 00:03:40.811
book was about castles and forts. Another

46
00:03:40.812 --> 00:03:45.314
was about famous kings and queens of the past. "Father

47
00:03:45.315 --> 00:03:49.986
Andrew would like that," Tom thought. "There

48
00:03:49.987 --> 00:03:55.881
are so many books here that I don't know where to start reading!" Just

49
00:03:55.882 --> 00:04:02.865
then he noticed Royal Court Etiquette: A Guide for the Young Prince .

50
00:04:02.866 --> 00:04:07.054
"That would be useful," Tom thought.

51
00:04:07.055 --> 00:04:10.363
He opened the book and turned the pages.

52
00:04:10.364 --> 00:04:16.760
The book covered everything from when to wear a crown to who should bow to whom.

53
00:04:16.761 --> 00:04:21.070
There was even a whole chapter on table settings.

54
00:04:21.071 --> 00:04:25.696
"Who knew there were so many types of silverware?"

55
00:04:25.697 --> 00:04:32.386
Tom pored over the illustrations of dessert spoons, salad forks, and steak knives.

56
00:04:32.387 --> 00:04:38.009
"I guess I should stop using my hands to eat."

57
00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:44.505
Tom soon grew bored with this chapter and turned to the section on armor.

58
00:04:44.506 --> 00:04:49.298
He took the book over to the prince's armor to compare it.

59
00:04:49.299 --> 00:04:55.923
Made of metal and covered with gold designs, Prince Edward's armor was beautiful to look at.

60
00:04:55.924 --> 00:04:59.161
But Tom wanted to do more than look at it.

61
00:04:59.162 --> 00:05:02.770
He wanted to try it on.

62
00:05:02.771 --> 00:05:08.435
"Prince Edward and I are the same size, so I know it'll fit me," he thought.

63
00:05:08.436 --> 00:05:13.899
"But I don't think I can get into it without help."

64
00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:19.731
Then he noticed the helmet and armor-covered gloves on a table.

65
00:05:19.732 --> 00:05:24.455
As Tom picked up a glove, a heavy metal disk fell out.

66
00:05:24.456 --> 00:05:27.986
"Well, that thing isn't mentioned in the book!"

67
00:05:27.987 --> 00:05:32.941
Tom watched the disk roll across the floor.

68
00:05:32.942 --> 00:05:37.974
"But it'll be perfect for cracking nuts."

69
00:05:37.975 --> 00:05:44.132
Tom left the disk on the floor while he put on the gloves.

70
00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:51.759
Then he put on the helmet and found his way to the mirror.

71
00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:55.519
It was hard to see through the slits for his eyes.

72
00:05:55.520 --> 00:06:01.984
"Phew! This helmet is much heavier and hotter than I expected," Tom thought.

73
00:06:01.985 --> 00:06:07.835
"I need to take it off." He tried to yank off the helmet, but . . .

74
00:06:07.836 --> 00:06:10.170
"Ahh!"

75
00:06:10.171 --> 00:06:17.914
It was stuck on his head!

